tasklist /FI "IMAGENAME eq Code.exe" | find /i "Code.exe"

If found, it will output the process details; otherwise, it will output "INFO: No tasks are running which match the specified criteria." So we can parse that. But we can just run a command that prints "Running" or "Not running". We can use a batch script: 

@echo off
tasklist /FI "IMAGENAME eq Code.exe" | find /i "Code.exe" >nul
if %errorlevel%==0 (
  echo VS Code is running
) else (
  echo VS Code is not running
)

But we can also do it in one line: 

